                        </div>
                        <!--/Single Image-->
                    </div>
                    <!--/Column-->

                    <!--Column-->
                    <div class="c-col-6">

                        <!--Single Image-->
                        <div class="single-image">

                            <img data-animation="slideRight" data-duration="1" data-color="#e3cdb6" class="has-anim"
                                alt="Single Image" src="../img/projects/studio23/gallery.jpeg">

                        </div>
                        <!--/Single Image-->

                    </div>
                    <!--/Column-->

                </div>
                <!--/Wrapper-->

                <!--Wrapper-->
                <div class="wrapper">

                    <!--Column-->
                    <div class="c-col-8">

                        <!--Text Wrapper-->
                        <div class="text-wrapper">

                            <h3 class="has-anim" data-stagger="0.1" data-duration="1.5" data-delay=".1"
                                data-animation="linesUp">
                                People have asked me, "Why did you start this? It seems so unrelated to your usual
                                work." Truth
                                is, that's exactly why I did it. This project is my way of stepping out of my comfort
                                zone. It's about challenging myself, exploring new territories. Sure, it might seem
                                random to others, but for me, it's a beautiful opportunity to grow and learn in
                                unfamiliar ways. It's scary and exciting - and that's precisely the point.
                            </h3>

                        </div>
                        <!--/Text Wrapper-->

                    </div>
                    <!--/Column-->

                </div>
                <!--/Wrapper-->

                <!--Wrapper-->
                <div class="wrapper">

                    <!--Column-->
                    <div class="c-col-12">

                        <!--Single Image-->
                        <div class="single-image">

                            <img data-animation="slideUp" data-duration="2" data-delay="0" data-color="#caaf9c"
                                class="has-anim" alt="Single Image" src="../img/projects/studio23/Vintgae.png">

                        </div>
                        <!--/Single Image-->

                    </div>
                    <!--/Column-->

                </div>
                <!--/Wrapper-->

                <!--Wrapper-->
                <div class="wrapper">

                    <!--Column-->
                    <div class="c-col-4"></div>
                    <!--/Column-->

                    <!--Column-->
                    <div class="c-col-8">

                        <!--Text Wrapper-->
                        <div class="text-wrapper">

                            <h4 style="color: rgba(25,27,29,.6)" class="has-anim" data-stagger="0.01" data-duration="1"
                                data-delay=".1" data-animation="wordsUp">
                                You know, whether this project succeeds or fails in the traditional sense isn't really
                                what matters to me. The true value lies in the incredible journey it's taking me on.
                                I've had the chance to connect with these amazingly talented artists, each with their
                                own unique vision and style. It's been eye-opening to see what art can do - how it can
                                convey complex emotions, challenge perspectives, and spark conversations. Every piece we
                                create tells a story, and being part of that narrative is incredible. The way art can
                                touch people, make them think, feel, and see the world differently - that's the real
                                magic here.
                            </h4>

                        </div>
                        <!--/Text Wrapper-->

                    </div>
                    <!--/Column-->

                </div>
                <!--/Wrapper-->

            </div>
            <!--/Section -->


            <!--Section-->
            <div class="section">

                <!--Wrapper-->
